{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ALX6VSus28Sh7jHicaup5h","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tImplement leave-service REST API with PostgreSQL backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone2 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** leave-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/leave-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Handle all leave request business logic including submission, approval, and rejection workflows\n- Calculate and enforce leave balance validation before accepting requests\n- Manage role-based access control distinguishing employee and manager permissions\n- Maintain audit trail for all leave request status changes with timestamps and manager comments\n- Provide REST API endpoints for leave types, balances, and request management\n- Calculate business days between start and end dates for leave requests\n- Persist all data to PostgreSQL database with proper schema and relationships\n- Query and filter leave requests by employee, manager, and status\n- Enforce manager authorization rules ensuring only direct managers can approve/reject\n- Maintain leave balance allocations and track used days per employee per leave type\n- Expose health check endpoint for service monitoring\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Validate start_date <= end_date and reject past dates\n- Implement atomic balance deduction during request creation and restoration on rejection\n- Prevent double-processing of leave requests (already approved/rejected)\n- Return appropriate HTTP status codes (404 for not found, 403 for unauthorized, 400 for validation errors)\n- Use UUIDs for all database primary keys\n- Seed initial data on startup for testing and demo purposes\n- Enable CORS headers to allow frontend communication\n- Implement proper error handling and logging to stdout\n- Use database transactions where needed to maintain data consistency\n- Structure code with clear separation of concerns (handlers, models, database layer)\n- Implement graceful shutdown to handle termination signals properly\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root of your component directory to declare endpoints and dependencies. Refer to the OpenChoreo workload configuration guidance in your skill for the correct format, endpoint types, dependency wiring, and the SPA nginx proxy pattern for frontend components.\n\nThe platform will handle git commit, push, build, and deploy automatically.\n## OpenAPI Spec\n\n```yaml\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Leave Management Service API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Backend service for leave request management\nservers:\n  - url: http://localhost:9090\npaths:\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health check endpoint\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Service is healthy\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    example: healthy\n  /api/leave-types:\n    get:\n      summary: Get all leave types\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave types\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: object\n                  properties:\n                    id:\n                      type: string\n                    name:\n                      type: string\n                    maxDays:\n                      type: integer\n  /api/employees/{employeeId}/balance:\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave balance for an employee\n      parameters:\n        - name: employeeId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave balance by type\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: object\n                  properties:\n                    leaveTypeId:\n                      type: string\n                    leaveTypeName:\n                      type: string\n                    allocated:\n                      type: integer\n                    used:\n                      type: integer\n                    remaining:\n                      type: integer\n        '404':\n          description: Employee not found\n  /api/leave-requests:\n    post:\n      summary: Submit a new leave request\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - employeeId\n                - leaveTypeId\n                - startDate\n                - endDate\n              properties:\n                employeeId:\n                  type: string\n                leaveTypeId:\n                  type: string\n                startDate:\n                  type: string\n                  format: date\n                endDate:\n                  type: string\n                  format: date\n                reason:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: Leave request created\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid request or insufficient balance\n        '500':\n          description: Server error\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave requests (filtered by query params)\n      parameters:\n        - name: employeeId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n        - name: managerId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n        - name: status\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n            enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave requests\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get a specific leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave request details\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/approve:\n    post:\n      summary: Approve a leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - managerId\n              properties:\n                managerId:\n                  type: string\n                comments:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request approved\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '403':\n          description: Manager not authorized\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n        '400':\n          description: Request already processed\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/reject:\n    post:\n      summary: Reject a leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - managerId\n              properties:\n                managerId:\n                  type: string\n                comments:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request rejected\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '403':\n          description: Manager not authorized\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n        '400':\n          description: Request already processed\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    LeaveRequest:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n        employeeId:\n          type: string\n        employeeName:\n          type: string\n        leaveTypeId:\n          type: string\n        leaveTypeName:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        numberOfDays:\n          type: integer\n        reason:\n          type: string\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n        managerId:\n          type: string\n        managerComments:\n          type: string\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n        updatedAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n```\n\n## Agent Instructions\nBuild a Go REST API service using net/http on port 9090 with PostgreSQL database. Implement database schema with four tables: leave_types (id, name, max_days), employees (id, name, manager_id), leave_balances (id, employee_id, leave_type_id, allocated, used), and leave_requests (id, employee_id, leave_type_id, start_date, end_date, number_of_days, reason, status, manager_id, manager_comments, created_at, updated_at). Create REST endpoints per OpenAPI spec: GET /health, GET /api/leave-types, GET /api/employees/{employeeId}/balance, POST /api/leave-requests with balance validation, GET /api/leave-requests with filters (employeeId, managerId, status), GET /api/leave-requests/{requestId}, POST /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/approve, POST /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/reject. Implement business logic: calculate business days between dates, validate sufficient leave balance before request creation, enforce manager authorization for approvals/rejections, maintain audit trail with timestamps, handle optimistic balance deduction on request submission and restoration on rejection. Seed database on startup with 3 leave types (Annual: 20 days, Sick: 10 days, Personal: 5 days), 5 employees (2 managers, 3 reports), and initial leave balances. Use lib/pq or pgx driver, github.com/google/uuid for IDs, enable CORS, structure code with handlers/models/db packages, implement graceful shutdown, and create multi-stage Dockerfile with golang:1.21-alpine. Database connection from DATABASE_URL environment variable.\n\n## General Constraints\n- Write ALL files in the current working directory (do NOT create files outside it).\n- The component must have a Dockerfile for containerized builds.\n- Implement the full API contract from the task — every endpoint must be functional.\n- Use the dependencies listed to understand what other services this component talks to.\n- The app MUST start without any required environment variables — use sensible hardcoded defaults for all config (JWT secrets, DB paths, API URLs, etc.). Environment variables may override defaults but must never be required.\n- Do NOT stub or mock — write real, working implementations.\n- Do NOT run, start, or execute the application server locally. Only write source files. The platform builds and deploys your code automatically — local execution is unnecessary and will cause port conflicts.\n- If you must run a quick compile check (e.g. `go build`, `tsc --noEmit`), do so without starting a server. Never use `go run`, `npm start`, `node server.js`, or any command that starts a long-running process.\n\n## Working Directory\nAll file operations must happen inside this directory:\n\n```\n/Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone2/leave-service\n```\n\nBefore you do anything else, navigate there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone2/leave-service\n```\n\nDo NOT create files outside this directory. Do NOT `cd` elsewhere during your work.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"156fdb1b-72d7-463b-a0e3-7a17384c7ff5","uuid":"a54cae15-dfbf-416f-aa2f-5b37881b3395","timestamp":"2026-05-02T20:01:12.774Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tImplement leave-service REST API with PostgreSQL backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone2 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** leave-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/leave-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Handle all leave request business logic including submission, approval, and rejection workflows\n- Calculate and enforce leave balance validation before accepting requests\n- Manage role-based access control distinguishing employee and manager permissions\n- Maintain audit trail for all leave request status changes with timestamps and manager comments\n- Provide REST API endpoints for leave types, balances, and request management\n- Calculate business days between start and end dates for leave requests\n- Persist all data to PostgreSQL database with proper schema and relationships\n- Query and filter leave requests by employee, manager, and status\n- Enforce manager authorization rules ensuring only direct managers can approve/reject\n- Maintain leave balance allocations and track used days per employee per leave type\n- Expose health check endpoint for service monitoring\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Validate start_date <= end_date and reject past dates\n- Implement atomic balance deduction during request creation and restoration on rejection\n- Prevent double-processing of leave requests (already approved/rejected)\n- Return appropriate HTTP status codes (404 for not found, 403 for unauthorized, 400 for validation errors)\n- Use UUIDs for all database primary keys\n- Seed initial data on startup for testing and demo purposes\n- Enable CORS headers to allow frontend communication\n- Implement proper error handling and logging to stdout\n- Use database transactions where needed to maintain data consistency\n- Structure code with clear separation of concerns (handlers, models, database layer)\n- Implement graceful shutdown to handle termination signals properly\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root of your component directory to declare endpoints and dependencies. Refer to the OpenChoreo workload configuration guidance in your skill for the correct format, endpoint types, dependency wiring, and the SPA nginx proxy pattern for frontend components.\n\nThe platform will handle git commit, push, build, and deploy automatically.\n## OpenAPI Spec\n\n```yaml\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Leave Management Service API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Backend service for leave request management\nservers:\n  - url: http://localhost:9090\npaths:\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health check endpoint\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Service is healthy\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    example: healthy\n  /api/leave-types:\n    get:\n      summary: Get all leave types\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave types\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: object\n                  properties:\n                    id:\n                      type: string\n                    name:\n                      type: string\n                    maxDays:\n                      type: integer\n  /api/employees/{employeeId}/balance:\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave balance for an employee\n      parameters:\n        - name: employeeId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave balance by type\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: object\n                  properties:\n                    leaveTypeId:\n                      type: string\n                    leaveTypeName:\n                      type: string\n                    allocated:\n                      type: integer\n                    used:\n                      type: integer\n                    remaining:\n                      type: integer\n        '404':\n          description: Employee not found\n  /api/leave-requests:\n    post:\n      summary: Submit a new leave request\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - employeeId\n                - leaveTypeId\n                - startDate\n                - endDate\n              properties:\n                employeeId:\n                  type: string\n                leaveTypeId:\n                  type: string\n                startDate:\n                  type: string\n                  format: date\n                endDate:\n                  type: string\n                  format: date\n                reason:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: Leave request created\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '400':\n          description: Invalid request or insufficient balance\n        '500':\n          description: Server error\n    get:\n      summary: Get leave requests (filtered by query params)\n      parameters:\n        - name: employeeId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n        - name: managerId\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n        - name: status\n          in: query\n          schema:\n            type: string\n            enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of leave requests\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get a specific leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Leave request details\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/approve:\n    post:\n      summary: Approve a leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - managerId\n              properties:\n                managerId:\n                  type: string\n                comments:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request approved\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '403':\n          description: Manager not authorized\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n        '400':\n          description: Request already processed\n  /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/reject:\n    post:\n      summary: Reject a leave request\n      parameters:\n        - name: requestId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              required:\n                - managerId\n              properties:\n                managerId:\n                  type: string\n                comments:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Request rejected\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LeaveRequest'\n        '403':\n          description: Manager not authorized\n        '404':\n          description: Request not found\n        '400':\n          description: Request already processed\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    LeaveRequest:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n        employeeId:\n          type: string\n        employeeName:\n          type: string\n        leaveTypeId:\n          type: string\n        leaveTypeName:\n          type: string\n        startDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        endDate:\n          type: string\n          format: date\n        numberOfDays:\n          type: integer\n        reason:\n          type: string\n        status:\n          type: string\n          enum: [pending, approved, rejected]\n        managerId:\n          type: string\n        managerComments:\n          type: string\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n        updatedAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n```\n\n## Agent Instructions\nBuild a Go REST API service using net/http on port 9090 with PostgreSQL database. Implement database schema with four tables: leave_types (id, name, max_days), employees (id, name, manager_id), leave_balances (id, employee_id, leave_type_id, allocated, used), and leave_requests (id, employee_id, leave_type_id, start_date, end_date, number_of_days, reason, status, manager_id, manager_comments, created_at, updated_at). Create REST endpoints per OpenAPI spec: GET /health, GET /api/leave-types, GET /api/employees/{employeeId}/balance, POST /api/leave-requests with balance validation, GET /api/leave-requests with filters (employeeId, managerId, status), GET /api/leave-requests/{requestId}, POST /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/approve, POST /api/leave-requests/{requestId}/reject. Implement business logic: calculate business days between dates, validate sufficient leave balance before request creation, enforce manager authorization for approvals/rejections, maintain audit trail with timestamps, handle optimistic balance deduction on request submission and restoration on rejection. Seed database on startup with 3 leave types (Annual: 20 days, Sick: 10 days, Personal: 5 days), 5 employees (2 managers, 3 reports), and initial leave balances. Use lib/pq or pgx driver, github.com/google/uuid for IDs, enable CORS, structure code with handlers/models/db packages, implement graceful shutdown, and create multi-stage Dockerfile with golang:1.21-alpine. Database connection from DATABASE_URL environment variable.\n\n## General Constraints\n- Write ALL files in the current working directory (do NOT create files outside it).\n- The component must have a Dockerfile for containerized builds.\n- Implement the full API contract from the task — every endpoint must be functional.\n- Use the dependencies listed to understand what other services this component talks to.\n- The app MUST start without any required environment variables — use sensible hardcoded defaults for all config (JWT secrets, DB paths, API URLs, etc.). Environment variables may override defaults but must never be required.\n- Do NOT stub or mock — write real, working implementations.\n- Do NOT run, start, or execute the application server locally. Only write source files. The platform builds and deploys your code automatically — local execution is unnecessary and will cause port conflicts.\n- If you must run a quick compile check (e.g. `go build`, `tsc --noEmit`), do so without starting a server. Never use `go run`, `npm start`, `node server.js`, or any command that starts a long-running process.\n\n## Working Directory\nAll file operations must happen inside this directory:\n\n```\n/Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone2/leave-service\n```\n\nBefore you do anything else, navigate there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone2/leave-service\n```\n\nDo NOT create files outside this directory. Do NOT `cd` elsewhere during your work.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
